invariant: INV-16
file: x25519_wide_edwards.h
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: equal_mask builds its mask from the bit as computed, with no read
  back from a volatile object. clang 23 for x86-64 then sees that the mask
  is all ones exactly when the digit's size is the entry's number, and it
  loads word 4 of each entry under a jump on that comparison: eight jumps
  on the digit in every scan. The values are right, so only the count of
  conditional branches on the x86-64 spec sees it (docs/decisions.md 148).

--- old
    volatile uint64_t differ = (uint64_t)(((ct_u128)(a ^ b) + UINT64_MAX) >> 64);
--- new
    uint64_t differ = (uint64_t)(((ct_u128)(a ^ b) + UINT64_MAX) >> 64);
